//! check: run(exit=1, stdout="error: missing")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: std.x.json, err.row, err.propagate
//!
//! `element`'s index-out-of-range row, ridden out of `main` so the
//! RECORD names it: the array has two elements and the index is one
//! past the end — the boundary value, because the boundary is where an
//! off-by-one would hide. The path addresses nothing, which is
//! `missing`, and it is a ROW where `List` indexing traps: the index
//! came out of a walk over a DOCUMENT, and §10 says data raises where a
//! caller's mistake traps.
//!
//! A negative index is the same miss by the same mechanism (the path
//! `"-1"` addresses nothing in an array); `element`'s doc says so and
//! `child_index`'s test holds the path it builds.
//!
//! Two lanes at this sprint's pin; lupin flips on a pin, not an edit
//! (see dom_navigation.lu).

use std.x.json

fn main() -> !int {
    let r = json.root("[10, 20]")?
    json.element(r, 2)?
    0
}
